  "job_B14.44_20251003_114316": {
    "text": "\u00d0egenes lagu: \u00d0egenlagu is, \u00fe\u00e6t he sy his bocrihtes wyr\u00f0e & \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0reo \u00f0inc of his lande do:\nEac of manegum landum mare landriht arist to cyniges gebanne, swilce is deorhege to cyniges hame &\nGeneates riht: Geneatriht is mistlic be \u00f0am \u00f0e on lande st\u00e6nt: on sumon he sceal landgafol syllan &\nKotsetlan riht: Kotesetlan riht be \u00f0am \u00f0e on lande stent: on sumon he sceal \u00e6lce Mond\u00e6ge ofer geares\nNe \u00f0earf he landgafol syllan.\nHim gebyria\u00f0 V \u00e6ceres to habbanne; mare, gyf hit on lande \u00f0eaw sy; & to lytel hit bi\u00f0, beo hit a\nSylle his heor\u00f0p\u00e6nig on halgan \u00d0unresd\u00e6g, ealswa \u00e6lcan frigean men gebyre\u00f0, & werige his hlafordes\nGebures gerihte: Geburgerihta syn mislice: gehwar hy syn hefige, gehwar eac medeme; On sumen lande\nHe sceal syllan on Michaeles m\u00e6ssed\u00e6ig X gafolp\u00e6niga & on Martinus m\u00e6ssed\u00e6g XXIII systra beres\n& he sceal licgan of Martinus m\u00e6ssan o\u00f0 Eastran \u00e6t hlafordes falde, swa oft swa him to beg\u00e6\u00f0.\n& of \u00f0am timan, \u00f0e man \u00e6rest ere\u00f0, o\u00f0 Martinus m\u00e6ssan he sceal \u00e6lcre wucan erian I \u00e6cer &\nHis gauolyr\u00f0e III \u00e6ceras erige & sawe of his aganum berne, & sylle his heor\u00f0p\u00e6nig & twegen &\nOn \u00f0am sylfum lande, \u00f0e \u00f0eos r\u00e6den on st\u00e6nt, gebure gebyre\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t him man to landsetene sylle II\nFor\u00f0ige ofer \u00fe\u00e6t gear ealle gerihtu, \u00f0e him to gebyrigean; & sylle him man tol to his weorce &\n\u00d0eos landlagu st\u00e6nt on suman lande; gehwar hit is, swa ic \u00e6r cw\u00e6\u00f0, hefigre, gehwar eac leohtre;\nOn sumen landa gebur sceal syllan huniggafol, on suman metegafol, on suman ealugafol.\nHede se \u00f0e scire healde, \u00fe\u00e6t he wite a, hw\u00e6t ealdlandr\u00e6den sy & hw\u00e6t \u00f0eode \u00f0eaw.\nBe \u00f0am \u00f0e beon bewita\u00f0: Beoceorle gebyre\u00f0, gif he gafolheorde healt, \u00fe\u00e6t he sylle \u00f0onne lande ger\u00e6d\nMid us is ger\u00e6d, \u00fe\u00e6t he sylle V sustras huniges to gafole; on suman landum gebyre\u00f0 mare gafolr\u00e6den.\nEac he sceal hwiltidum geara beon on manegum weorcum to hlafordes willan, toeacan benyr\u00f0e &\n& gyf he wel gelend bi\u00f0, he sceal beon gehorsad, \u00fe\u00e6t he m\u00e6ge to hlafordes seame \u00fe\u00e6t syllan o\u00f0\u00f0e sylf\n& fela \u00f0inga swa gerad man sceal don; eal ic nu atellan ne m\u00e6ig.\n\u00d0onne him for\u00f0si\u00f0 gebyrige, hede se hlaford \u00f0\u00e6s he l\u00e6fe, bute hwet friges sy.\nGafolswane: Gafolswane gebyre\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he sylle his slyht, be \u00f0am \u00f0e on lande stent.\nOn manegum landum stent, \u00fe\u00e6t he sylle \u00e6lce geare XV swyn to sticunge, X ealde & V gynge h\u00e6bbe\nGyme eac swan, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6fter sticunge his slyhtswyn wel behweorfe s\u00e6ncge: \u00f0onne bi\u00f0 he ful wel\nEac he sceal beon swa ic \u00e6r be beocere cw\u00e6\u00f0 oftr\u00e6de to gehwilcon weorce & gehorsad to hlafordes\n\u00d0eow swan & \u00f0eow beocere \u00e6fter for\u00f0si\u00f0e be anre lage wyr\u00f0e.\nBe \u00e6hteswane: \u00c6hteswane, \u00f0e inheorde healt, gebyre\u00f0 stifearh & his gewirce, \u00f0onne he spic behworfen\nBe manna metsunge: Anan esne gebyre\u00f0 to metsunge XII pund godes cornes & II scip\u00e6teras & I god\nBe wifmonna metsunge: \u00d0eowan wifmen: VIII pund cornes to mete, I sceap o\u00f0\u00f0e III p\u00e6niga to\nEallum \u00e6htemannum gebyre\u00f0 Midwintres feorm & Eastorfeorm, sulh\u00e6cer & h\u00e6rfesthandful toeacan\nBe folgeran: Folgere gebyre\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he on twelf mon\u00f0um II \u00e6ceras geearnige, o\u00f0erne gesawene & o\u00f0erne\nGyf he mare geearnian m\u00e6ig, him bi\u00f0 sylfum fremu.\nBe s\u00e6dere: S\u00e6dere gebyre\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6bbe \u00e6lces s\u00e6dcynnes \u00e6nne leap fulne, \u00f0onne he \u00e6lc s\u00e6d wel\nBe oxanhyrde: Oxanhyrde mot l\u00e6swian II oxan o\u00f0\u00f0e ma mid hlafordes heorde on gem\u00e6nre l\u00e6se be his\n& his metecu mot gan mid hlafordes oxan.\nBe kuhyrde: Cuhyrde gebyre\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6bbe ealdre cu meolc VII niht, sy\u00f0\u00f0an heo nige cealfod h\u00e6f\u00f0,\n& ga his metecu mid hlafordes cu.\nBe sceaphyrdan: Sceaphyrdes riht is, \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6bbe twelf nihta dingan to Middanwintra & I lamb of\nBe gathyrde: Gathyrde gebyre\u00f0 his heorde meolc ofer Martinus m\u00e6ssed\u00e6ig, & \u00e6r \u00f0am his d\u00e6l hw\u00e6ges\nBe cyswyrhte: Cyswyrhtan gebyre\u00f0 hundred cyse, & \u00fe\u00e6t heo of wringhw\u00e6ge buteran macige to\nBe berebrytte: Berebryttan gebyre\u00f0 corngebrot on h\u00e6rfeste \u00e6t bernes dure, gif him his ealdorman ann,\nBe bydele: Bydele gebyra\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he for his wycan sy weorces frigra \u00f0onne o\u00f0er man; for\u00f0an he sceal\nEac him gebyre\u00f0 sum landsticce for his geswince.\nBe wudewarde: Wuduwearde gebyre\u00f0 \u00e6lc windfylled treow.\nH\u00e6igwerde gebyre\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t man his geswinces lean gecnawe on \u00f0am endum, \u00f0e to etenl\u00e6se licgan;\nHwilces landsticces geann, \u00fe\u00e6t sceal beon mid folcrihte nyhst etenl\u00e6se; for\u00f0am gyf he for sl\u00e6w\u00f0e his\nGyf he \u00f0onne eal wel gefri\u00f0a\u00f0, he healdan sceal, \u00f0onne bi\u00f0 he godes leanes ful wel wyr\u00f0e.\nLandlaga syn mistlice, swa ic \u00e6r beforan s\u00e6de.\nNe sette we na \u00f0as gerihtu ofer ealle \u00f0eoda, \u00f0e we \u00e6r beforan ymbe spr\u00e6con; ac we cy\u00f0a\u00f0, hw\u00e6t\nGyf we selre geleornia\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t we willa\u00f0 georne lufian & healdon, be \u00f0\u00e6re \u00f0ede \u00f0eawe, \u00f0e we \u00f0\u00e6nne\nFor\u00f0am laga sceal on leode luflice leornian, lof se \u00f0e on lande sylf nele leosan.\nFeola syndon folcgerihtu: on sumre \u00f0eode gebyre\u00f0 winterfeorm, Easterfeorm, bendform for ripe,\n\u00d0is is \u00f0eah myngung manna biwiste & eal \u00fe\u00e6t ic \u00e6r beforan ymberehte.",
